Subject: Competitive play: a player who leaves a set's search ends it for both
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A set's two games search RANKED for each other (0056). When one player left
that search with Back, nothing told the other game: it searched on until the
server gave up on the set. SHOnlineMatchmakingDraft's Back now tells the
module (src/platform/competitive_match.cpp), whose host withdraws the
player's Ready to play! at once; the other game's host sees the set called
off within seconds. A game whose set is called off during its search (0058)
now leaves the online menus as well, the way the online menu's LOG OUT does
(Pop, its sound, TransitionOnlineMatchToMainMenu, as the draft's own error
path does for an error that needs a new login), instead of stopping in the
RANKED menu; the host says why on its card.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_competitive.h b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
--- a/include/mscharged_competitive.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
@@ -78,6 +78,12 @@
 #endif
 
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// The RANKED search screen: the player's Back left the search. A set's game
+// tells the opponent's, which leaves the set (tweak patch 0063).
+void mscharged_competitive_search_back(void);
+#endif
+
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
 // The set's players by their profile names (tweak patch 0059): the game shows
 // its online players by their Mii names (at most 10 characters, also what the
 // network carries). An online player row's name text `name` (a
